# Kaini B — the Kaini voice (patches/kaini.patch) with measured fixes:
#   - mono: back-to-back notes re-strike from the envelope's current level
#     instead of from zero, so the line flows without dipping between notes
#   - sub 0.25: the voice sat ~5 dB light under 150 Hz
#   - cutoff 640 -> 520 (key tracking stays 1, so the movement stays):
#     the voice ran ~12 dB hot in the upper mids
#   - tape for its wow only (the pitch smear the chorus alone can't
#     give); no wear, so no tape hiss and no dropouts
#   - chorus_hiss 0.3: the BBD floor ~10 dB down, as on a quiet chip
#   - a shorter filter decay (0.45 s) so every mono re-strike blooms
#     again, but a smaller, slightly slower sweep (0.8 oct, 20 ms): a dark
#     rest under a big fast sweep reads as brass, most of all on short
#     notes, which hear only the sweep
#   - effects matched to how the original's image moves (it sways at
#     0.78 Hz, only ~2.6 dB deep, with as much note-to-note motion as
#     slow swirl): a slow, shallow chorus II (0.39 Hz LFO — the image
#     moves at twice the LFO rate — depth 0.1) instead of one deep, regular
#     swirl, and a more present dark room (pre-delay 20 ms) that gives each
#     note its own reflections; width 1.6 brings L/R correlation to ~0.65
#   - stronger velocity-to-level, so accents in the MIDI read as accents
waveform 2
circuit 0
key_track 1
cutoff 520
resonance 0.65
drive 0.5
filter_env 0.8
filter_attack 0.02
filter_decay 0.45
filter_sustain 0
filter_release 0.1
attack 0.012
decay 1
sustain 1
release 0.1
chorus_mode 2
chorus_rate 0.39
chorus_depth 0.1
volume 0.849
octave 3
mono 1
sub 0.25
vel_amp 0.9
vel_filter 0.8
tape_wow 0.1
tape_flutter 0.03
tape_age 0
reverb_wet 0.3
reverb_decay 0.55
reverb_tone 3500
width 1.6
chorus_hiss 0.3
reverb_pre 0.02
